From 545eeea09b08a6a2fe9ba823a40f97b43123dcd0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 11:11:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Test and document the sparse solvers of MAGMA

MAGMASolversTest (on a GPU, with the device cpu or the device of the GPU
of MFEM, sequential and parallel) solves the Laplace equation with each
Krylov solver of MAGMA, without preconditioner and with each
preconditioner of MAGMA, then a second operator and an operator of
another size, the right hand side being given to MAGMA or copied; checks
the initial guess (iterative_mode), a null right hand side, the report of
each solver stopped by the maximum number of iterations, the effect of the
dimensions of the Krylov space of GMRES and of the shadow space of IDR,
the failure of the setup with a null diagonal entry (collective in
parallel), and the refusal of invalid options; and applies the
preconditioners of MAGMA with the conjugate gradient of MFEM, compared with
the Jacobi smoother and the incomplete LU factorization of MFEM, in
sequential and on the diagonal blocks in parallel. QMR of MAGMA, without
look-ahead, breaks down on this system without preconditioner: it is only
run with the Jacobi and incomplete LU preconditioners. The generic test
runs the entries of MAGMA on CUDA and HIP GPUs.
